==Trivia==
*The Σ in her Evolved Form's name is the Greek letter "sigma".
**Σ was later reused for [[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa, type Σ]].
*The designs on her lab coat reference [[wikipedia:Skeletal formula|skeletal formula]], a common way to represent molecules where bonds are shown as lines.
*Both of Wise Empress Nobel, Type Σ's icons depict three rings at the base of the antennae-like parts of her headphones, something not seen in-battle as they merely use a coloured version of the design seen in her Normal Form. The antennae also appear slightly longer in her Evolved Form's icons while her flask is somewhat opaque, but again neither of those details are reflected in her in-battle appearance.
*[[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Lilin]]'s design may have been inspired by hers, considering how they are both scientists working on making a potion. Both of their attack animations also show a single drop of liquid exploding.
**Lilin's Japanese Evolved and [[True Form]] descriptions also imply that her potion is supposed to be a love potion.
*Wise Empress Nobel, type Σ, [[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa, type Σ]], and [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars, type Φ]] are the only Galaxy Gals to use uppercase Greek symbols in their evolved form instead of lowercase ones.

